From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:39:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: give the ISP DART its
 address filter ranges

isp_dart0 describes its dapf registers, and since "iommu: apple-dart:
take the coprocessor DARTs through a firmware suspend" a DART with a
dapf reg reads apple,dapf-ranges to write the filter back after a sleep.
isp_dart0 had no ranges, so the DART failed to probe with -EINVAL and
apple-isp found no IOMMU (-ENODEV): on the first J604 boot with the ISP
enabled by the boot loader, the camera did not bind.

Add the 13 ranges of the ADT's dart-isp dapf-instance-0, decoded as the
boot loader's t8110 DAPF records (start, end, last word 1, config 0x31),
in record order. The J604 and J713 ADTs of macOS 25G83 and 26B123 carry
the same records.

Fixes: 3ba1e5403625 ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the ISP and its DARTs")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit de5617eca1e141430c26eca34aef9ef17ec073ac)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index d34dd727ec..612edce266 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -1433,6 +1433,24 @@
 			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 387 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			power-domains = <&ps_isp_sys>;
 			apple,remap-streams = <1 0>, <2 0>, <3 0>, <6 0>, <7 0>, <10 0>, <11 0>;
+			/*
+			 * The ADT dart-isp dapf-instance-0 records in order, bounds as
+			 * the loader writes them; each record's last word is 1. The
+			 * J604 and J713 ADTs (25G83 and 26B123) give the same 13.
+			 */
+			apple,dapf-ranges = /bits/ 64 <0x380704000 0x380704063>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x380730000 0x380733fff>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x380e3c000 0x380e3c003>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x39062c000 0x390648003>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x501660000 0x501660003>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x220004000 0x2200162fc>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x220044000 0x2200562fc>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x2201c4000 0x2201d62fc>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x222004000 0x2220162fc>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x222044000 0x2220562fc>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x2221c4000 0x2221d62fc>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x3803c0000 0x3803e4000>,
+					    /bits/ 64 <0x382824000 0x382824004>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
